Template: amp-panel/enabled-devices
Type: multiselect
Choices: local, remote, oba, oba3
Choices-C: local, remote, oba, oba3
Default: local, remote, oba, oba3
Description: Devices available in Amp Panel:
 XML views cover local/DI and remote/DI stations and EDFA OBA/OBA3.
 The external daemon must refresh status.xml.

Template: amp-panel/admin-username
Type: string
Default: admin
Description: Administrator username:
 This is the first Amp Panel administrator account.

Template: amp-panel/auth-mode
Type: select
Choices: RADIUS server, Local passwords on this device
Choices-C: radius, local
Default: radius
Description: Browser authentication method:
 RADIUS verifies passwords on a separate authentication server. Local passwords
 are stored as salted password hashes on this device.

Template: amp-panel/local-admin-password
Type: password
Description: Local administrator password:
 This password is used only when local authentication is selected. It is stored
 only as a salted password hash.

Template: amp-panel/port
Type: string
Default: 8000
Description: Web interface TCP port:
 The panel runs without root privileges, so choose a port from 1024 to 65535.

Template: amp-panel/data-dir
Type: string
Default: /var/lib/amp-panel
Description: Directory for the SQLite database and persistent state:
 Use /var/lib/amp-panel, or an absolute path below /mnt, /media or /srv.
 Existing data in the selected directory is preserved.

Template: amp-panel/radius-server
Type: string
Description: RADIUS server hostname or IP address:

Template: amp-panel/radius-port
Type: string
Default: 1812
Description: RADIUS authentication UDP port:

Template: amp-panel/radius-secret
Type: password
Description: RADIUS shared secret:

Template: amp-panel/mdns-hostname
Type: string
Description: Local mDNS hostname, without .local:

Template: amp-panel/unconfigured
Type: note
Description: Amp Panel was installed but is not configured
 Required settings were not supplied. The services remain disabled. Run
 "sudo amp-panel configure" from a terminal to finish the configuration.

Template: amp-panel/xml-status-file
Type: string
Default: /var/lib/amp-panel/status.xml
Description: Path to status.xml refreshed by the device daemon:
 The panel only reads this file. It does not modify it.

Template: amp-panel/xml-control-file
Type: string
Default: /var/lib/amp-panel/control.xml
Description: Path to control.xml consumed by the device daemon:
 The panel validates and atomically replaces this file. The device should only
 read it and acknowledge the request in status.xml.
